    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Items are sorted by weight, with heavier goods at the bottom of boxes. Lighter, delicate items are placed on top.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p>After packing, the team secures the contents in the truck using tie‑downs, straps, and protective blankets. The truck is then loaded in a specific sequence: heavy, low‑profile items first, followed by mid‑weight boxes, and finally delicate items on top. This layered strategy prevents crushing and keeps fragile goods isolated.</p>

<p>During transit, the driver follows the pre‑planned route, taking advantage of the truck’s built‑in shock absorbers and climate control. Movers monitor the load at key points, ensuring that no items shift during the journey.</p>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Upon arrival, the uncrating process begins.</p>
